import re

p5_prose = """<p>Memory consolidation transforms labile, newly encoded neural representations into stable, long-lasting memory traces through two distinct temporal phases: synaptic consolidation and systems consolidation. Synaptic consolidation occurs locally at dendritic synapses within minutes to hours following encoding. This fast cellular process requires intracellular calcium cascades, protein kinase activation, immediate-early gene transcription (e.g., c-Fos, Zif268), and de novo protein synthesis to structurally stabilize expanded dendritic spines. Infusion of protein synthesis inhibitors (such as anisomycin) into the hippocampus during this critical time window permanently arrests synaptic stabilization.</p>
<p>Systems consolidation operates on a macroscopic circuit level, reorganizing memory networks over weeks, months, or years. According to the Standard Model of Consolidation, newly encoded declarative representations depend obligatorily on the hippocampus to bind distributed neocortical sensory traces. Over time, repeated coordinated replay—predominantly during slow-wave sleep (SWS), characterized by hippocampal sharp-wave ripples (SWRs) synchronized with neocortical slow oscillations and thalamocortical spindles—gradually strengthens direct cortico-cortical connections. Eventually, remote memories become independent of the hippocampus and are stored within distributed neocortical networks, including the anterior cingulate cortex (ACC) and prefrontal cortex.</p>
<p>To investigate synaptic and systems dynamics, neuroscientists trained adult rats in contextual fear conditioning (CFC), where a novel chamber is paired with mild footshocks. Cohorts received either pharmacological protein synthesis inhibition (intra-hippocampal anisomycin immediately or 6 hours post-training) or optogenetic silencing of excitatory pyramidal neurons in dorsal CA1 (hippocampus) or the anterior cingulate cortex (ACC) during retrieval tests administered at Day 1 (recent memory) or Day 30 (remote memory). Freezing behavior (indexing fear memory retrieval) and immediate-early gene c-Fos expression in the ACC were quantified (Table 1).</p>"""

p_texts = re.findall(r"<p>(.*?)</p>", p5_prose, re.DOTALL)
prose = re.sub(r"<[^>]+>", " ", " ".join(p_texts))
words = prose.split()
print("Word count:", len(words))
